{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semiconductor doping semiconductor doping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md","fileName":"Semiconductor Doping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semiconductor Doping","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 21:06\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Semiconductor and Integrated Circuit History]] [[Photovoltaic Cell Physics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Semiconductor and Integrated Circuit History","Photovoltaic Cell Physics","Semiconductor Band Gap","N-Type Semiconductor","P-Type Semiconductor","P-N Junction","computing.epub","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semiconductor doping semiconductor doping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md","fileName":"Semiconductor Doping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semiconductor Doping","heading":"Semiconductor Doping","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Semiconductor doping introduces controlled impurities into a crystal to change how electrical charge moves through it. P-type material supports mobile positive holes, while N-type material supports mobile electrons.\n\nJoining differently doped regions creates the electrical behavior needed for transistors and other devices. Precise control of impurity concentration is essential for repeatable chip production.\n\nIn a photovoltaic junction, impurities introduce allowed energy levels inside the [[Semiconductor Band Gap]]. Donor levels near the conduction band make [[N-Type Semiconductor]] material rich in mobile electrons; acceptor levels near the valence band make [[P-Type Semiconductor]] material rich in holes. The kind and amount of impurity therefore affect the conductivity of both sides of a [[P-N Junction]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Semiconductor and Integrated Circuit History","Photovoltaic Cell Physics","Semiconductor Band Gap","N-Type Semiconductor","P-Type Semiconductor","P-N Junction","computing.epub","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semiconductor doping semiconductor doping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semiconductor Doping.md","fileName":"Semiconductor Doping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semiconductor Doping","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[computing.epub]]\n[[directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Semiconductor and Integrated Circuit History","Photovoltaic Cell Physics","Semiconductor Band Gap","N-Type Semiconductor","P-Type Semiconductor","P-N Junction","computing.epub","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}